course: dictionary
lesson: 6732
title: A piece of a word, or a name?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: On its own, «ola» is not an English word. You will usually find it as a piece of a longer word, such as «cola», «granola» or «Coca-Cola». When you see a fragment like this, look at the whole word around it to work out what it belongs to.
explain: «So Ola's brother has 3 sisters, one more than Ola has.» Here the capital O and the apostrophe s tell you that Ola is a name, a girl's name. The sentence is about people, so the clues point to a name, not a word for a thing.
explain: «If Ola has 2 sisters, there are 3 girls in the family: Ola and her 2 sisters.» Read the numbers carefully. Ola is one of the three girls, and she has two sisters. Always check your answer by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: «Ola» is not an English word on its own.
fact: «Ola» can be a piece of a longer word, such as «cola», «granola» or «Coca-Cola».
fact: «Ola» is also a girl's name.
fact: In Spanish, «hola» means hello, and the h is silent. Without the h, «ola» means wave, as a wave of the sea.
fact: «Ola» is also the name of a taxi company in India and of a brand.
exercise: «So Ola's brother has 3 sisters, one more than Ola has.» How many sisters does Ola have? | 1 | 4 | *2 | 3
exercise: «If Ola has 2 sisters, there are 3 girls in the family: Ola and her 2 sisters.» How many girls are in the family? | 5 | 4 | 2 | *3
exercise: Which longer word can «ola» be a piece of? | Pencil | Table | Window | *Granola
test: In Spanish, «ola» (without the h) means what, when you talk about the sea? | Sand | Bird | Hello | *Wave
test: «Ola» is the name of a taxi company in which country? | *India | Japan | Spain | Brazil
exam: You see «ola» on its own in a word list. What is the most likely reason? | It is always a plural of a longer English word | *It is a piece split from a longer word, like cola or granola, or it is a name | It is a random sound with no meaning | It is a new English word that means hello
